(** * planb4_calib_chain_step_n24: the Laurent chains of planb4_g1_poleA/poleB 24 cut into 10 block certificates: point 24 carries K = 3n+1 = 73 stepper steps per channel, split into blocks of widths [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1].  For each channel and block i, a remainder-state literal (block 0 stays symbolic: the numerator state planb4_g1_shp/shm 24) and one Example: the w_i-step readout from that state equals its literal, closed by one vm_compute bite over w_i steps.  A build consumer assembles these through planb4_calib_chain_glue_laur instead of re-biting the whole chain.

    Mission.  the Laurent chains of planb4_g1_poleA/poleB 24 cut into 10 block certificates: point 24 carries K = 3n+1 = 73 stepper steps per channel, split into blocks of widths [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 1].  For each channel and block i, a remainder-state literal (block 0 stays symbolic: the numerator state planb4_g1_shp/shm 24) and one Example: the w_i-step readout from that state equals its literal, closed by one vm_compute bite over w_i steps.  A build consumer assembles these through planb4_calib_chain_glue_laur instead of re-biting the whole chain.

    Dependencies.  zzm1_gauss (zzId carrier); planb4_g1_laur_extract (planb4_g1_laur_go, planb4_g1_shp, planb4_g1_shm, planb4_g1_denw); stdlib QArith, List.

